  {
   "label": "Gathering Hymn",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "eyebrow",
     "text": "Gathering Hymn"
    },
    {
     "type": "h2",
     "text": "O Come, O Come, Emmanuel"
    },
    {
     "type": "rubric",
     "text": "TIS 265",
     "margin": "16px 0 22px"
    },
    {
     "type": "hymn",
     "verses": [
      [
       "O come, O come, Emmanuel,",
       "and ransom captive Israel,",
       "that mourns in lonely exile here",
       "until the Son of God appear.",
       "Rejoice! Rejoice!",
       "Emmanuel shall come to you,",
       "O Israel."
      ],
      [
       "O come, O come, great Lord of might,",
       "who to the tribes on Sinai’s height",
       "in ancient times did give the law",
       "In cloud and majesty and awe.",
       "Rejoice! Rejoice!",
       "Emmanuel shall come to you,",
       "O Israel."
      ],
      [
       "O come, O Key of David, come,",
       "and open wide our heavenly home;",
       "make safe the way that leads on high,",
       "and close the path to misery.",
       "Rejoice! Rejoice!",
       "Emmanuel shall come to you,",
       "O Israel."
      ],
      [
       "O come, O branch of Jesse, free",
       "your own from Satan’s tyranny;",
       "from depths of hell your people save,",
       "and give them victory o’er the grave.",
       "Rejoice! Rejoice!",
       "Emmanuel shall come to you,",
       "O Israel."
      ],
      [
       "O come, O day-spring, come and cheer",
       "our spirits by your advent here;",
       "disperse the gloomy clouds of night,",
       "And death’s dark shadows put to flight",
       "Rejoice! Rejoice!",
       "Emmanuel shall come to you,",
       "O Israel."
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "note",
     "text": "CCLI Licence #309884"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "label": "Gathering",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "eyebrow",
     "text": "Gathering in God’s Name"
    },
    {
     "type": "h2",
     "text": "Greeting"
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "We are gathered in the name",
      "of Christ, for whom we wait.",
      [
       "Amen.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "The Lord be with you",
      [
       "And also with you",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "h3",
     "text": "Welcome & Introduction"
    },
    {
     "type": "h3",
     "text": "Call to Worship"
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "We worship with Christians near and far,",
      [
       "waiting together for the coming of Christ.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "God’s word is for all of us.",
      [
       "May it be a lamp to our feet",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "and a light to our path.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "Christ, for whom we wait,",
      "speak to us",
      "that we may hear you at the door.",
      [
       "Move among us",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "that we may behold your coming glory.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "Receive our prayers",
      [
       "that we may learn to wait",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "with hope and courage.",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "Amen.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "h3",
     "text": "Lighting the Advent Wreath"
    },
    {
     "type": "rubric",
     "text": "The first candle is lit."
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "God of the long night,",
      "as we light this first candle",
      "we keep watch for your coming.",
      "Make us faithful doorkeepers,",
      "awake to your knock and ready to open.",
      "Come, Lord Jesus.",
      [
       "Come, Lord Jesus.",
       "all"
      ]
     ],
     "margin": "0"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "label": "Receiving God’s Mercy",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "eyebrow",
     "text": "Receiving God’s Mercy"
    },
    {
     "type": "h2",
     "text": "Invitation to Confession"
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "In Advent we wait for the One",
      "who comes to set all things right."
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "Trusting in God’s mercy,",
      "let us bring to God the times",
      "we have slept when we should have watched,",
      "kept silent when we should have spoken,",
      "and made ourselves the centre",
      "when we should have pointed to Christ."
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "h3",
     "text": "Confession"
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      [
       "Loving God,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "we admit that we have done wrong:",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "in our thoughts, words, and actions.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      [
       "Please forgive us.",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "Help us to change,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "and guide us in the future.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      [
       "Help us to live justly,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "to show mercy,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "and to walk humbly with you.",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "Amen.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "h3",
     "text": "Absolution"
    },
    {
     "type": "rubric",
     "text": "Rev Glen proclaims God’s mercy, and everyone responds:"
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      [
       "Amen",
       "all"
      ]
     ],
     "margin": "0"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "label": "Giving Praise",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "eyebrow",
     "text": "Gathering in God’s Name"
    },
    {
     "type": "h2",
     "text": "Giving Praise"
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "We give thanks to you, faithful God,",
      [
       "for you keep watch over your world",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "and never grow weary.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "You spoke through the prophets,",
      [
       "comforting your people in exile",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "and making a way in the wilderness.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "In Jesus you came among us,",
      "light shining in the darkness,",
      [
       "and you will come again",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "to make all things new.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "By your Spirit you keep us awake in hope",
      [
       "and make room in us for your love.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "We give you thanks and praise,",
      [
       "now and always. Amen.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "h3",
     "text": "Prayer of the Day"
    },
    {
     "type": "rubric",
     "text": "The Prayer of the Day is said, and everyone responds:"
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      [
       "Amen",
       "all"
      ]
     ],
     "margin": "0"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "label": "Isaiah 64",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "eyebrow",
     "text": "Bible and Teaching"
    },
    {
     "type": "h2",
     "text": "Readings"
    },
    {
     "type": "rubric",
     "text": "Readings are from the Common English Bible.",
     "margin": "16px 0 0"
    },
    {
     "type": "worktitle",
     "text": "Isaiah 64:1–9",
     "margin": "22px 0 18px",
     "sub": "First reading"
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "A reading from the prophet Isaiah."
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "If only you would tear open the heavens and come down!",
      "Mountains would quake before you",
      "like fire igniting brushwood or making water boil.",
      "If you would make your name known to your enemies,",
      "the nations would tremble in your presence."
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "When you accomplished wonders beyond all our expectations;",
      "when you came down, mountains quaked before you.",
      "From ancient times,",
      "no one has heard,",
      "no ear has perceived,",
      "no eye has seen any god but you",
      "who acts on behalf of those who wait for him!",
      "You look after those who gladly do right;",
      "they will praise you for your ways.",
      "But you were angry when we sinned;",
      "you hid yourself when we did wrong.",
      "We have all become like the unclean;",
      "all our righteous deeds are like a menstrual rag.",
      "All of us wither like a leaf;",
      "our sins, like the wind, carry us away.",
      "No one calls on your name;",
      "no one bothers to hold on to you,",
      "for you have hidden yourself from us,",
      "and have handed us over to our sin."
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "But now, Lord, you are our father.",
      "We are the clay, and you are our potter.",
      "All of us are the work of your hand.",
      "Don’t rage so fiercely, Lord;",
      "don’t hold our sins against us forever,",
      "but gaze now on your people, all of us."
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "This is the word of the Lord",
      [
       "Thanks be to God",
       "all"
      ]
     ],
     "margin": "0"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "label": "Gospel",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "eyebrow",
     "text": "Bible and Teaching"
    },
    {
     "type": "h2",
     "text": "Gospel"
    },
    {
     "type": "worktitle",
     "text": "Mark 13:24–37",
     "margin": "22px 0 18px"
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      {
       "segments": [
        [
         "Alleluia! ",
         ""
        ],
        [
         "Alleluia!",
         "all"
        ]
       ]
      },
      {
       "segments": [
        [
         "Show us your faithful love, Lord! Give us your salvation! ",
         ""
        ],
        [
         "Alleluia!",
         "all"
        ]
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "The Lord be with you",
      [
       "And also with you",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "A reading from the Good News of Jesus Christ according to Mark.",
      [
       "Glory to you Lord Jesus Christ",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "prose",
     "paragraphs": [
      "“In those days, after the suffering of that time, the sun will become dark, and the moon won’t give its light. The stars will fall from the sky, and the planets and other heavenly bodies will be shaken. Then they will see the Human One coming in the clouds with great power and splendor. Then he will send the angels and gather together his chosen people from the four corners of the earth, from the end of the earth to the end of heaven."
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "prose",
     "paragraphs": [
      "“Learn this parable from the fig tree. After its branch becomes tender and it sprouts new leaves, you know that summer is near. In the same way, when you see these things happening, you know that he’s near, at the door. I assure you that this generation won’t pass away until all these things happen. Heaven and earth will pass away, but my words will certainly not pass away."
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "prose",
     "paragraphs": [
      "“But nobody knows when that day or hour will come, not the angels in heaven and not the Son. Only the Father knows. Watch out! Stay alert! You don’t know when the time is coming. It is as if someone took a trip, left the household behind, and put the servants in charge, giving each one a job to do, and told the doorkeeper to stay alert. Therefore, stay alert! You don’t know when the head of the household will come, whether in the evening or at midnight, or when the rooster crows in the early morning or at daybreak. Don’t let him show up when you weren’t expecting and find you sleeping. What I say to you, I say to all: Stay alert!”"
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "This is the good news of the Lord",
      [
       "Praise to you Lord Jesus Christ",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "h3",
     "text": "Sermon",
     "margin": "0"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "label": "Affirmation",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "eyebrow",
     "text": "Ministry of the Word"
    },
    {
     "type": "h2",
     "text": "Affirmation"
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      [
       "We believe in God the Father,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "whose love gives room for creation,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "whose mercy restores all,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "and whose promise holds creation fast.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      [
       "We believe in Christ,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "through whom all creation is made—",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "the Word made flesh,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "friend of the outcast,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "light in the darkness,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "risen and true.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      [
       "We believe in the Spirit",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "who moves among us,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "who brings life to dust,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "stirs courage,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "kindles compassion,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "and weaves us into one.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      [
       "We believe the Church is a living body,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "open to all,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "rooted in grace,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "and sent to serve in love.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      [
       "This is our faith,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "our calling,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "our love.",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "Amen.",
       "all"
      ]
     ],
     "margin": "0"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "label": "Prayers & Peace",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "eyebrow",
     "text": "Prayers and Peace"
    },
    {
     "type": "h2",
     "text": "Intercessions"
    },
    {
     "type": "rubric",
     "text": "Led by the intercessor. Everyone responds to each petition with:"
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "Lord in your mercy",
      [
       "Hear our prayer",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "h3",
     "text": "Prayer for St Aidan’s"
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      [
       "God of Mission,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "you call us to share your love.",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "Send your Holy Spirit to guide us",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "in deepening our discipleship,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "in welcoming everyone,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "and in sharing your love with courage.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      [
       "Help St Aidan’s grow",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "in faith, diversity,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "and service to our community.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "h3",
     "text": "Conclusion to Prayers"
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "Loving God, you hear our prayers.",
      [
       "By your Spirit,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "guide us to live with open hearts,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "trusting in your presence",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "and grace,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "through Jesus Christ our Lord.",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "Amen.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "h3",
     "text": "Greeting of Peace"
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "We are the body of Christ",
      [
       "His Spirit is with us",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "The peace of the Lord be with you",
      [
       "And also with you",
       "all"
      ]
     ],
     "margin": "0"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "label": "Offertory Hymn",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "eyebrow",
     "text": "Offertory Hymn"
    },
    {
     "type": "h2",
     "text": "The Advent of Our God"
    },
    {
     "type": "rubric",
     "text": "TIS 271",
     "margin": "16px 0 22px"
    },
    {
     "type": "hymn",
     "verses": [
      [
       "The advent of our God,",
       "with eager prayers we greet,",
       "and singing hasten on his road",
       "his coming reign to meet."
      ],
      [
       "The everlasting Son",
       "was born to make us free;",
       "and he a servant’s form put on",
       "to gain our liberty."
      ],
      [
       "Let Zion now arise",
       "to greet her infant king,",
       "and gladly take with thankful heart",
       "the peace he comes to bring"
      ],
      [
       "As judge, on clouds of light,",
       "he soon will come again,",
       "his scattered people to unite,",
       "with them in heaven to reign."
      ],
      [
       "Then evil flee away",
       "before the rising dawn!",
       "Let our old nature day by day",
       "God’s image still put on."
      ],
      [
       "Praise to the incarnate Son",
       "who comes to set us free,",
       "with Father, Spirit, ever one",
       "to all eternity."
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "note",
     "text": "CCLI Licence #309884"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "label": "Introduction to Communion",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "eyebrow",
     "text": "Holy Communion"
    },
    {
     "type": "h2",
     "text": "Introduction to Communion"
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "Come to this table,",
      "where Christ who is coming",
      "meets us already in bread and wine."
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "Here those who wait are fed,",
      "and we taste the kingdom",
      "that is drawing near."
     ],
     "margin": "0"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "label": "Preface",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "eyebrow",
     "text": "The Thanksgiving Prayer"
    },
    {
     "type": "h2",
     "text": "Holy Communion"
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "The Lord be with you.",
      [
       "And also with you",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "Lift up your hearts.",
      [
       "We lift them to the Lord.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "Let us give thanks to the Lord our God.",
      [
       "It is right to give our thanks and praise.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "It is right to give you thanks,",
      "God of every age."
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "You created the world in love,",
      "and you keep watch over it",
      [
       "through every night.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "When your people were lost in exile,",
      "you did not abandon them.",
      "Through prophets you spoke comfort",
      [
       "and made a way in the wilderness.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "In Jesus, born of Mary,",
      "you came to make your home among us,",
      "and you will come again in glory",
      "to make all things new.",
      [
       "In you we wait with hope.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "So with all who keep watch,",
      "and with all who long for your coming,",
      "we give you thanks and praise,",
      "saying together:",
      [
       "Blessed is the One who comes,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "whose light is dawning",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "and whose love makes room for all.",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "Blessed is our God, forever.",
       "all"
      ]
     ],
     "margin": "0"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "label": "Words of Institution",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "eyebrow",
     "text": "The Thanksgiving Prayer"
    },
    {
     "type": "h2",
     "text": "Bread"
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "On the night of his giving,",
      "Jesus blessed and broke the bread.",
      "He shared it with his friends, saying:",
      "Take and eat.",
      "This is my body, broken for you.",
      "As you do this, you are remembering me.",
      [
       "Lord my God.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "h3",
     "text": "Wine"
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "After they had eaten,",
      "he took the cup of wine,",
      "gave thanks, and said:",
      "Drink this, all of you.",
      "This is my blood of the new covenant,",
      "poured out for you and for all,",
      "to reconcile and to heal.",
      "As you do this, you are remembering me.",
      [
       "Lord my God.",
       "all"
      ]
     ],
     "margin": "0"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "label": "Acclamation to Sanctus",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "eyebrow",
     "text": "The Thanksgiving Prayer"
    },
    {
     "type": "h2",
     "text": "Mystery of Faith"
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "Let us proclaim the mystery of faith.",
      [
       "Christ has died to set us free.",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "Christ is risen to make us whole.",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "Christ will come again",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "with justice and joy.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "Come, Holy Spirit,",
      "rest upon these gifts of bread and wine,",
      "that they may be for us",
      "the life of Christ.",
      [
       "As we share this meal,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "make us one with each other,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "and one in Christ, our risen Lord",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "Gathered with angels and archangels,",
      "and with every generation",
      "who has trusted your love,",
      "we join the hymn of heaven:",
      [
       "Holy, holy, holy Lord,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "God of power and might,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "Heaven and earth are full of your glory.",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "Praise to you in the highest.",
       "all"
      ]
     ],
     "margin": "0"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "label": "Lord’s Prayer to Invitation",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "eyebrow",
     "text": "Holy Communion"
    },
    {
     "type": "h2",
     "text": "The Lord’s Prayer"
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      [
       "Father, uphold the holiness of your name.",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "Bring in your kingdom.",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "Give us the bread we need for today.",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "Forgive us our sins,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "for we also forgive everyone who has wronged us.",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "And save us in times of trial.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      [
       "For you are worthy,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "our Lord and God,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "to receive glory and honour and power,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "because you created all things.",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "Amen.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "h3",
     "text": "Breaking the Bread"
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "We break and share this bread,",
      "a sign of Christ’s life",
      "poured out for us.",
      [
       "Though we are many, we are made one,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "for we all eat of the one bread.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "h3",
     "text": "Invitation to Communion"
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "The gifts of God for the people of God.",
      [
       "Graciously nourish us, O Christ,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "so that we who try to follow you",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "may receive food for the journey",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "and be bound in solidarity",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "with all who walk in your way",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "Amen.",
       "all"
      ]
     ],
     "margin": "0"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "label": "Communion Anthem",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "eyebrow",
     "text": "Communion Anthem"
    },
    {
     "type": "h2",
     "text": "Jesus Christ, Be the Wine of Grace"
    },
    {
     "type": "rubric",
     "text": "Sung by all",
     "margin": "16px 0 22px"
    },
    {
     "type": "hymn",
     "verses": [
      [
       "In the singing, in the silence,",
       "in the hands expectant, open,",
       "in the blessing, in the breaking,",
       "in the presence at this table",
       "Jesus Christ, Jesus Christ,",
       "be the wine of grace.",
       "Jesus Christ, Jesus Christ,",
       "be the bread of peace."
      ],
      [
       "In the question, in the answer,",
       "in the moment of acceptance,",
       "in the heart’s cry, in the healing,",
       "in the circle of your people.",
       "Jesus Christ, Jesus Christ,",
       "be the wine of grace.",
       "Jesus Christ, Jesus Christ,",
       "be the bread of peace."
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "note",
     "text": "CCLI Licence #309884"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "label": "Receiving Communion",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "eyebrow",
     "text": "Receiving Communion"
    },
    {
     "type": "h2",
     "text": "Christ Be Our Light"
    },
    {
     "type": "rubric",
     "text": "SoG 787 · verses 1, 3, 4 & 5 with chorus",
     "margin": "16px 0 22px"
    },
    {
     "type": "hymn",
     "verses": [
      [
       "Longing for light, we wait in darkness",
       "Longing for truth, we turn to You.",
       "Make us Your own, Your holy people",
       "Light for the world to see."
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "rubric",
     "text": "Chorus"
    },
    {
     "type": "hymn",
     "verses": [
      [
       "Christ, be our light!",
       "Shine in our hearts.",
       "Shine through the darkness.",
       "Christ, be our light!",
       "Shine in Your church gathered today."
      ],
      [
       "Longing for food, many are hungry",
       "Longing for water, many still thirst.",
       "Make us Your bread, broken for others",
       "Shared until all are fed."
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "rubric",
     "text": "Chorus"
    },
    {
     "type": "hymn",
     "verses": [
      [
       "Christ, be our light!",
       "Shine in our hearts.",
       "Shine through the darkness.",
       "Christ, be our light!",
       "Shine in Your church gathered today."
      ],
      [
       "Longing for shelter, many are homeless",
       "Longing for warmth, many are cold.",
       "Make us Your building, sheltering others",
       "Walls made of living stone."
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "rubric",
     "text": "Chorus"
    },
    {
     "type": "hymn",
     "verses": [
      [
       "Christ, be our light!",
       "Shine in our hearts.",
       "Shine through the darkness.",
       "Christ, be our light!",
       "Shine in Your church gathered today."
      ],
      [
       "Many the gift, many the people",
       "Many the hearts that yearn to belong.",
       "Let us be servants to one another",
       "Making Your kingdom come."
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "rubric",
     "text": "Chorus"
    },
    {
     "type": "hymn",
     "verses": [
      [
       "Christ, be our light!",
       "Shine in our hearts.",
       "Shine through the darkness.",
       "Christ, be our light!",
       "Shine in Your church gathered today."
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "note",
     "text": "CCLI Licence #309884"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "label": "Sending Out",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "eyebrow",
     "text": "Sending Out God’s People"
    },
    {
     "type": "h2",
     "text": "Prayer after Communion"
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "Faithful God,",
      "you have fed us at your table",
      "with a foretaste of the kingdom",
      "that is coming."
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "Send us out to keep watch,",
      "to prepare the way,",
      "to point to your light,",
      "and to carry your love into the world,",
      "until Christ comes in glory."
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "h3",
     "text": "Gratitude for Communion"
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      [
       "Lord,",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "we have broken your bread",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "and received your life.",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "By the power of your Spirit",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "keep us always in your love",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "through Jesus Christ our Lord.",
       "all"
      ],
      [
       "Amen.",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "h3",
     "text": "This Week at St Aidan’s"
    },
    {
     "type": "rubric",
     "text": "Notices",
     "margin": "0"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "label": "Blessing & Dismissal",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "eyebrow",
     "text": "Sending Out God’s People"
    },
    {
     "type": "h2",
     "text": "Blessing"
    },
    {
     "type": "rubric",
     "text": "Rev Glen pronounces God’s blessing, and everyone responds:"
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      [
       "Amen",
       "all"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "h3",
     "text": "Dismissal"
    },
    {
     "type": "lines",
     "lines": [
      "As we await our coming Saviour,",
      "go in peace, to love and serve the Lord.",
      [
       "In the name of Christ. Amen.",
       "all"
      ]
     ],
     "margin": "0"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "label": "Sending Hymn",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "eyebrow",
     "text": "Sending Hymn"
    },
    {
     "type": "h2",
     "text": "Lo! He Comes with Clouds Descending"
    },
    {
     "type": "rubric",
     "text": "TIS 273",
     "margin": "16px 0 22px"
    },
    {
     "type": "hymn",
     "verses": [
      [
       "Lo! He comes with clouds descending,",
       "Once for favored sinners slain;",
       "Thousand thousand saints attending,",
       "Swell the sound of this refrain:",
       "Hallelujah! Hallelujah! Hallelujah!",
       "God appears on earth to reign."
      ],
      [
       "Every eye shall now behold Him",
       "Robed in awesome majesty;",
       "Those who have betrayed and sold Him,",
       "Pierced and nailed Him to the tree,",
       "Deeply shamed before him,",
       "deeply shamed before him,",
       "deeply shamed before him,",
       "Shall the true Messiah see."
      ],
      [
       "The dear tokens of His passion",
       "Still His dazzling body bears;",
       "Cause of endless exultation",
       "To His ransomed worshippers;",
       "With what rapture, with what rapture,",
       "with what rapture,",
       "Gaze we on those glorious scars!"
      ],
      [
       "Sing, Amen! Let all adore you,",
       "High on your eternal throne;",
       "Savior, take the power and glory,",
       "Claim the kingdom for your own;",
       "O come quickly! O come quickly!",
       "O come quickly!",
       "Hallelujah! Come Lord, come!"
      ]
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "note",
     "text": "CCLI Licence #309884"
    }
   ]
  }
 ]
}